Come on! Keep it together, dammit!

36
00:02:38,360 --> 00:02:39,360
Geez!

37
00:02:39,360 --> 00:02:41,360
Mr. Uzui!

38
00:02:41,360 --> 00:02:42,360
Huh?

39
00:02:42,360 --> 00:02:43,360
Hey!

40
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:44,860
That you, Kamado?

41
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:47,360
Long time no see, kid.

42
00:02:48,360 --> 00:02:49,360
Yes.

43
00:02:49,860 --> 00:02:51,360
It's good to see you again.

44
00:02:51,360 --> 00:02:53,860
I'm so glad you've recovered, Mr. Uzui.

45
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:55,360
Ha!

46
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:57,860
Well, I don't know if you can call this recovered.

47
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:03,360
I hear you managed to take on another upper rank.

48
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:06,360
You should count yourself lucky to have all your limbs intact.

49
00:03:06,860 --> 00:03:07,860
I certainly do.

50
00:03:07,860 --> 00:03:09,860
I'm just thankful I managed to survive.

51
00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:10,860
Right.

52
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:11,860
Now then.

53
00:03:11,860 --> 00:03:14,860
Are you ready to work off all that rust you've built up?

54
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:15,860
Yes!

55
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:16,860
I can't wait!

56
00:03:16,860 --> 00:03:17,860
I can't wait!

57
00:03:17,860 --> 00:03:43,400
Hey!

58
00:03:44,340 --> 00:03:45,580
Good to see you!

59
00:03:45,980 --> 00:03:47,060
Tanjiro, you're back!

60
00:03:47,060 --> 00:03:48,400
Well, it's about time.

61
00:03:48,920 --> 00:03:49,760
It's been a while.

62
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:50,880
It's good to see you.

63
00:03:51,320 --> 00:03:53,180
Thank you for all that you did for me.

64
00:03:53,640 --> 00:03:55,580
Hey, what's with all the formality, huh?

65
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:57,740
We should be the ones who are thanking you.

66
00:03:58,160 --> 00:03:59,560
Training must be going well.

67
00:04:00,040 --> 00:04:00,460
Mm-hmm.

68
00:04:00,720 --> 00:04:01,720
You look manly.

69
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:05,140
You guys need to be eating a lot more!

70
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:09,040
If you don't eat, the afternoon session will be even harder!

71
00:04:09,420 --> 00:04:09,900
What?

72
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:12,060
If you don't finish your meal,

73
00:04:12,280 --> 00:04:14,500
I'll just have to add more drills to the session.

74
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:15,720
We'll eat!

75
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:16,500
We'll eat!

76
00:04:16,500 --> 00:04:19,140
Guess I will too!

77
00:04:19,540 --> 00:04:19,820
Eda!

78
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:21,900
Please, have as much as you want!

79
00:04:22,280 --> 00:04:22,760
Great!

80
00:04:23,020 --> 00:04:24,040
Thanks for the meal!

81
00:04:25,080 --> 00:04:26,840
If you boys don't empty this pot,

82
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:29,200
Lord Tengen is gonna tack on more drills!

83
00:04:32,700 --> 00:04:35,500
Listen, you're taking care of patrol tonight, right?

84
00:04:35,920 --> 00:04:36,260
Yeah.

85
00:04:36,900 --> 00:04:37,860
Wanna switch with me?

86
00:04:38,340 --> 00:04:39,360
Not a chance!

87
00:04:39,360 --> 00:04:41,480
Cause if you go on night patrol,

88
00:04:41,480 --> 00:04:44,280
you get to be excused from training the next morning.

89
00:04:44,280 --> 00:04:44,780
Aww...

90
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:45,280
Jeez.

91
00:04:51,600 --> 00:04:52,000
Jeez.

92
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:52,240
Jeez.

93
00:04:52,240 --> 00:05:06,180
We sure haven't been seeing any demons lately, have we?

94
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:09,640
That fact alone is enough to make my skin crawl.

95
00:05:10,640 --> 00:05:11,280
Get this.

96
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:14,420
I hear it's because the demons are searching for a girl named Nezuko.

97
00:05:15,800 --> 00:05:17,720
That's just speculation, isn't it?

98
00:05:18,980 --> 00:05:21,940
It's not like anyone actually asked a demon in person.

99
00:05:21,940 --> 00:05:24,340
Well, yeah, that's true.

100
00:05:25,340 --> 00:05:29,100
But wouldn't it be great if they were gone and it was like this forever?

101
00:05:29,460 --> 00:05:31,120
That's probably wishful thinking.

102
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:35,060
I mean, demon slaying has been going on for a thousand years now.

103
00:05:35,060 --> 00:05:42,180
Hey, where'd you go?

104
00:05:54,220 --> 00:05:58,020
Who knows, one could pop up like this any moment.

105
00:05:58,880 --> 00:06:00,140
Don't be such a jerk!

106
00:06:00,440 --> 00:06:00,880
Sorry.

107
00:06:01,380 --> 00:06:01,900
My bad.

108
00:06:05,060 --> 00:06:12,520
Hey, enough is enough, okay?

109
00:06:12,960 --> 00:06:14,500
We have to stay focused.

110
00:06:14,860 --> 00:06:15,260
Okay.

111
00:06:35,060 --> 00:06:40,680
Right, time for the next drill.

112
00:06:41,060 --> 00:06:42,300
Split up into pairs.

113
00:06:43,680 --> 00:06:44,860
Here I go.

114
00:06:46,780 --> 00:06:48,260
So fast.

115
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:54,140
Come on now, show me what you're made of, damn it!

116
00:07:05,060 --> 00:07:10,260
So there's no way you can fight an upper rank, unless you have stamina like that?

117
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:18,740
Those upper ranks are insanely strong, right?

118
00:07:19,400 --> 00:07:21,480
You wouldn't believe the stuff they can do.

119
00:07:21,820 --> 00:07:23,140
But what was it like?

120
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:25,500
Well, let's see.

121
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:28,860
There'd be a POW and you'd already be hit.

122
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:33,020
But the fact that you're not dead means you could respond in time to turn around,

123
00:07:33,020 --> 00:07:35,360
only to get slammed by them again.

124
00:07:35,680 --> 00:07:37,380
Then you feel a big crunch.

125
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:40,180
And if that cuts off the oxygen to your brain...

126
00:07:40,180 --> 00:07:41,260
All right, that's enough.

127
00:07:41,400 --> 00:07:42,240
I think we get it.

128
00:07:42,780 --> 00:07:46,780
Sounds like it's a world far beyond the comprehension of us ordinary folks.

129
00:07:47,240 --> 00:07:47,680
Mm-hmm.

130
00:07:50,720 --> 00:07:51,740
All right.

131
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,260
To wrap things up for today, let me see.

132
00:07:56,500 --> 00:07:57,820
You're hitting that mountain.

133
00:07:58,180 --> 00:08:00,300
Take a lap around its foot and come back.

134
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:01,000
What?

135
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:04,120
If you don't get a move on, you're not gonna eat!

136
00:08:05,780 --> 00:08:08,700
Come on, guys, run like you mean it!

137
00:08:08,840 --> 00:08:12,080
If you can't even take this, you're not gonna cut it!

138
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:15,060
He means well.

139
00:08:15,420 --> 00:08:17,060
Lord Tengen has a way with words.

140
00:08:17,580 --> 00:08:18,500
Sure does.

141
00:08:18,680 --> 00:08:20,320
But he's actually a softie.

142
00:08:20,720 --> 00:08:24,000
Just the other day, he refused to even eat his meal.

143
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:25,860
Until the last Slayer came back.

144
00:08:26,180 --> 00:08:28,480
In the end, he went all the way to the mountain to get him.

145
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:32,780
You know I heard all of that, right?

146
00:08:34,720 --> 00:08:39,940
The Master put these swordsmen in my care, so I'm not about to let them burn out under my watch.

147
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:41,360
Of course not.

148
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:44,560
I'll be heading out, then.

149
00:08:44,860 --> 00:08:45,540
Sounds good.

150
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:46,820
That'll get you warmed up.

151
00:08:52,740 --> 00:08:57,360
Everyone with the potential to become a Hashira is kind deep down inside.

152
00:08:57,360 --> 00:09:01,600
Excuse me.

153
00:09:01,740 --> 00:09:03,400
Can I have another tray, please?

154
00:09:03,700 --> 00:09:04,520
You got it.

155
00:09:05,440 --> 00:09:07,260
I can't take much more of this.

156
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,980
But I've got to win.

157
00:09:10,020 --> 00:09:12,620
Or I won't be able to keep my promise to the Master.

158
00:09:12,620 --> 00:09:17,600
I've got to do all I can to keep pushing forward.

159
00:09:17,980 --> 00:09:19,920
So, Mr. D, you will join us.

160
00:09:21,800 --> 00:09:22,860
Can I get another?

161
00:09:23,820 --> 00:09:24,840
You got it.

162
00:09:26,260 --> 00:09:30,680
So if I lose, I have to agree to come back and take part in the training, right?

163
00:09:31,460 --> 00:09:33,640
But does that mean I don't have to if I win?

164
00:09:34,360 --> 00:09:34,800
What?

165
00:09:35,860 --> 00:09:37,080
Well, that's not...

166
00:09:37,080 --> 00:09:38,840
Here you go.

167
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:40,460
One for you, too.

168
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:44,060
Mister, please bring him another one.

169
00:09:44,360 --> 00:09:45,120
Will do.

170
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:50,340
After this tray, I'm calling it quits.

171
00:09:51,420 --> 00:09:54,360
Meaning, if you eat that extra order of noodles,

172
00:09:54,980 --> 00:09:56,640
you'll have defeated me in this battle.

173
00:09:57,540 --> 00:10:00,400
And if I take part in the Hashira training after that,

174
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:02,700
you'll be satisfied then, right?

175
00:10:03,460 --> 00:10:05,000
Yes, very much!

176
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,860
All right, then finish your noodles.

177
00:10:08,480 --> 00:10:09,040
Right!

178
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:13,920
Mr. Giyu, I'm sure that you could go on eating.

179
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:21,940
Even so, I feel like I'm about to burst any second now!

180
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:41,680
Sorry, I'm a bit late.

181
00:10:42,620 --> 00:10:44,600
Well, I only just got here myself.

182
00:10:45,420 --> 00:10:47,620
So then, how goes the training?

183
00:10:48,620 --> 00:10:53,540
Never in a million years could I see them becoming assets in a fight against an upper rank.

184
00:10:53,540 --> 00:10:58,520
Yeah, you could say the same thing about mine.

185
00:10:59,420 --> 00:11:03,520
However, training all the core members is what the Master has asked of us.

186
00:11:04,460 --> 00:11:04,980
Yeah.

187
00:11:06,240 --> 00:11:08,760
So, what is it you wanted at this hour?

188
00:11:11,020 --> 00:11:13,580
It's just... it's been bugging me all this time.

189
00:11:13,580 --> 00:11:17,360
You mean what happened back at that castle?

190
00:11:20,500 --> 00:11:23,080
You and I drove the demons to the brink together,

191
00:11:23,340 --> 00:11:25,180
but just before we dispatched them,

192
00:11:25,600 --> 00:11:27,860
they were able to vanish in the blink of an eye.

193
00:11:27,860 --> 00:11:33,860
That many disappearing so quickly

194
00:11:33,860 --> 00:11:36,760
is certainly something worth at least looking into.

195
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:37,720
Yeah.

196
00:11:38,860 --> 00:11:41,640
I've been pondering that myself since then.

197
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:44,880
What could be behind that door that shut on us?

198
00:11:45,660 --> 00:11:48,140
That there might actually be a demon hideout

199
00:11:48,140 --> 00:11:50,660
that we still don't know about.

200
00:11:51,340 --> 00:11:52,680
A demon hideout, huh?

201
00:11:52,680 --> 00:11:56,080
I've been back to that castle several times since then,

202
00:11:56,640 --> 00:11:58,440
only to come up empty every time.

203
00:11:59,320 --> 00:12:01,000
It was right around then

204
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:04,400
that demons suddenly vanished from the cities all at once.

205
00:12:05,020 --> 00:12:08,040
So what they're after is Kamado's kid sister.

206
00:12:09,040 --> 00:12:11,480
I have no doubt in my mind that's the case,

207
00:12:12,160 --> 00:12:15,380
which leads me to believe something big is about to happen soon.

208
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:17,080
Huh.

209
00:12:18,040 --> 00:12:19,500
Well, whenever that starts,

210
00:12:20,220 --> 00:12:22,300
I'll be happy to bring it all to an end.

211
00:12:22,680 --> 00:12:26,240
Don't you think this might be a bad omen

212
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:28,660
for everyone here in the Demon Slayer Corps?

213
00:12:31,600 --> 00:12:33,680
So long as I'm training the Corps members,

214
00:12:33,820 --> 00:12:35,460
it keeps me distracted from it all.

215
00:12:36,380 --> 00:12:39,400
But I look at the situation with a dispassionate eye,

216
00:12:39,860 --> 00:12:41,320
and I can't help but be aware

217
00:12:41,320 --> 00:12:43,080
of the inevitable battle that's to come.

218
00:12:44,540 --> 00:12:46,480
That this calm we're experiencing

219
00:12:46,480 --> 00:12:52,280
might be the harbinger of a storm like no other.

220
00:12:53,680 --> 00:12:56,200
Worrying about it isn't going to get us anywhere, though.

221
00:12:57,380 --> 00:12:58,760
While I have you here,

222
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:00,480
I do have a proposal for you.

223
00:13:01,040 --> 00:13:01,420
Heh.

224
00:13:02,440 --> 00:13:04,740
Well, I happen to have one for you, too.

225
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:07,200
Let me go ahead and tell you mine first.

226
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:11,420
Take me on in a match, Higuro!

227
00:13:11,420 --> 00:13:13,720
What a coincidence.

228
00:13:14,260 --> 00:13:16,840
That's exactly what I was going to propose to you.

229
00:13:16,840 --> 00:13:22,980
I'm leaving it here, all right?

230
00:13:22,980 --> 00:13:24,540
Oh, thanks, Tanjiro.

231
00:13:24,780 --> 00:13:25,540
That's perfect.

232
00:13:26,140 --> 00:13:27,440
Here, drink this.

233
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:29,860
It's high-quality gyokuro tea.

234
00:13:30,200 --> 00:13:31,980
It helps with recovering from fatigue.

235
00:13:32,240 --> 00:13:32,740
Really?

236
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:34,800
Don't mind if I do.

237
00:13:38,580 --> 00:13:39,200
Delicious!

238
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:41,160
Listen, Tanjiro,

239
00:13:41,160 --> 00:13:42,760
we've been wanting to thank you

240
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:44,440
for what you did at the Entertainment District.

241
00:13:44,820 --> 00:13:45,880
Thank you so much!

242
00:13:46,120 --> 00:13:46,420
Huh?

243
00:13:46,760 --> 00:13:48,100
We're extremely grateful.

244
00:13:48,560 --> 00:13:49,160
Oh, but...

245
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:51,000
it wasn't just me,

246
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:51,980
so I don't deserve it.

247
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:55,000
Right, it was you and your younger sister.

248
00:13:55,620 --> 00:13:56,700
That boar-headed kid

249
00:13:56,700 --> 00:13:58,080
and the young man with the yellow hair.

250
00:13:58,920 --> 00:14:00,200
And, of course, Lord Tengen.

251
00:14:00,680 --> 00:14:02,740
If even one of you hadn't been there,

252
00:14:03,120 --> 00:14:04,300
I don't think we could have seen

253
00:14:04,300 --> 00:14:05,560
the sunrise that morning.

254
00:14:06,420 --> 00:14:08,200
For Lord Tengen and all three of us

255
00:14:08,200 --> 00:14:09,380
to have made it back alive,

256
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:12,180
when it seemed impossible at one point.

257
00:14:12,860 --> 00:14:14,340
It almost had to be a miracle.

258
00:14:16,240 --> 00:14:16,600
Higuro.

259
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:19,380
But the truth is,

260
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:21,320
Lord Tengen still wants to keep fighting.

261
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:23,660
She's right.

262
00:14:24,060 --> 00:14:25,560
He even calls out in his sleep.

263
00:14:25,560 --> 00:14:28,260
He's been blaming himself

264
00:14:28,260 --> 00:14:29,780
for leaving the Corps.

265
00:14:31,140 --> 00:14:31,900
Tanjiro,

266
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:34,660
please defeat Muzanki Butsuji.

267
00:14:36,420 --> 00:14:37,140
Right.

268
00:14:37,600 --> 00:14:38,280
I will.

269
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:45,920
All right, everybody!

270
00:14:46,340 --> 00:14:47,100
Listen up!

271
00:14:47,720 --> 00:14:49,020
Today, I'm calling off

272
00:14:49,020 --> 00:14:50,440
the long-distance mountain run

273
00:14:50,440 --> 00:14:51,940
that we usually finish up with.

274
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:53,520
In its place

275
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:55,080
will be a special drill

276
00:14:55,080 --> 00:14:56,560
